", "# Feature: rank_ace_proportion\n# Feature description: Proportion of the rank of Ace (1) in the total card rank sum.\n# Usefulness: Gauges how dominant Ace is as a contributor to the overall rank, key for assessing hand strength in Royal Flush considerations.\ndf['rank_ace_proportion'] = df['low_card_rank'] / df['card_rank_sum']", "# Dropping potentially redundant or highly correlated columns:\n# Usefulness: Removes features that provide little to no new information due to redundancy or high correlation with another feature.\ndf.drop(columns=['is_flush', 'card_rank_sum'], inplace=True)", "# Feature: pair_proportion\n# Feature description: Proportion of pairs in the total number of unique ranks.\n# Usefulness: Provides an intuitive measure of pair dominance within the hand.\ndf['pair_proportion'] = df['pair_count'] / df['rank_unique_count']", "# Feature: normalized_rank_range\n# Feature description: Ratio of rank range to the maximum possible rank range (12).\n# Usefulness: Normalizes the range of ranks in comparison to the total possible range, making the feature scale-invariant.\ndf['normalized_rank_range'] = df['rank_range'] / 12", "# Feature: harmonic_mean_rank\n# Feature description: Harmonic mean of the ranks of the five cards.\n# Usefulness: Gives more weight to smaller ranks, complementing the average rank feature for analysis.\nfrom scipy.stats import hmean\ndf['harmonic_mean_rank'] = hmean(df[['V2', 'V4', 'V6', 'V8', 'V10']], axis=1)"]
